          "collection_date": "2022-10",
          "description": {
            "comment": "We studied the microbial composition of a thermal stream in Navoi Region, Uzbekistan. The aim of our project was to isolate autotrophic microorganisms. Samples of water, sediments and microbial mats were collected in October 2022, from a water stream formed by discharge of artesian groundwater located in Navoiy Region, Uzbekistan (40.16226 N, 66.0,1274 E). The stream was 1.5-2.0 m wide and had a temperature 62.5C at the discharge point and above 40C throughout its current of up to 50-55 m. Samples were taken along the stream into sterile 50 mL tubes and transported to the laboratory, where they were prepared for microbiological and geochemical studies.",
